  "question": {
    "text": "An electron in the hydrogen atom initially in the fourth excited state makes a transition to $\\mathrm{n}^{\\text {th }}$ energy state by emitting a photon of energy 2.86 eV. The integer value of $n$ will be ____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{E}=13.6\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_1^2}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_1^2}\\right)$<br/>$2.86=13.6\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}^2}-\\frac{1}{5^2}\\right)$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}^2}=0.21+\\frac{1}{2.5} \\\\ & \\mathrm{n}^2=4 \\\\ & \\mathrm{n}=2\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}